# ==========================================================================
# CardDemo repository Git attributes.
#
# Purpose: guarantee byte-exact preservation of the legacy mainframe DATA
# artifacts retained under legacy/data/**. These files are migration
# authorities: their exact bytes (EBCDIC encoding, packed COMP-3 fields,
# fixed-width record layouts) are the contract the Java re-platform is
# validated against. Git end-of-line normalization or text filtering would
# silently corrupt them, so their handling is pinned here explicitly.
#
# CI hash verification: the SHA-256 of every file under legacy/data/** and
# legacy/catlg/LISTCAT.txt is recorded in docs/traceability-matrix.md
# (Data-Artifact Inventory). Continuous integration should recompute and
# compare those hashes on every build to prove the authorities remain
# unmodified. See docs/onboarding/pitfalls.md ("Never edit legacy bytes").
# ==========================================================================

# --- EBCDIC physical-sequential datasets ---------------------------------
# Pure binary: EBCDIC code page + binary packed-decimal (COMP-3) content.
# `binary` == `-text -diff`, so Git performs no EOL conversion and shows no
# textual diff, keeping every byte identical across clone / checkout / commit.
legacy/data/EBCDIC/AWS.M2.CARDDEMO.*        binary

# --- ASCII fixed-width seed data -----------------------------------------
# Human-readable, so keep textual diffs, but disable EOL conversion: a CRLF
# injection would shift every fixed-width column by one byte per line and
# break the fixed-position load contract. `-text` prevents any normalization.
legacy/data/ASCII/*.txt                     -text

# --- VSAM catalog listing -------------------------------------------------
# Reference report; keep as text with no EOL conversion for stable hashing.
legacy/catlg/LISTCAT.txt                    -text
